  "name": "Nubian music (Egyptian-Sudanese Nile Valley)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Nubian music of the Mahas and Kunuz communities of the Nile Valley between Aswan and Dongola, with post-1964 Aswan High Dam relocation extending diaspora to Cairo and Khartoum. Performance integrates Nubian-language responsorial chorus with tar frame-drum and darbuka, plus twentieth-century urban-oud incorporation. Modal vocabulary draws on Nile Valley pentatonic-leaning tradition with distinct Nubian intervals. The post-1964 diaspora produced an exile-mourning lyric corpus addressing the loss of villages submerged by Lake Nasser. The aragid wedding-dance repertoire constitutes the core ceremonial layer.",
